    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "The (α, β)-approximation regret of the CUCB algorithm in n rounds using an (α, β)-approximation oracle is at most sum_{i∈[m],∆imin>0}( 6 ln n·∆imin/(f^{-1}(∆imin))^2 + ∫_{∆imin}^{∆imax} 6 ln n/(f^{-1}(x))^2 dx ) + (π^2/3 + 1)·m·∆max, where f(·) is the bounded smoothness function."
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Regret is n·α·β·opt − E[sum r_mu(S_t)], i.e. (alpha,beta)-approximation pseudo-regret; mapped to alpha_regret. Simplified version Eq.(4): (6 ln n/(f^{-1}(Delta_min))^2 + pi^2/3+1)·m·Delta_max is proved in the text. Classical MAB special case gives sum 6 ln n/Delta_i + (pi^2/3+1) m Delta_max (Eq. 11)."
